# Skip browser checks on small changes

Browser snapshots of this site are huge, because the page holds every hidden pane. Each one is billed as input.

Do not open the browser, take snapshots, or take screenshots to verify small changes:

- copy and text edits ("our" to "your", removing a line)
- renaming a button or label
- CSS tweaks: colors, spacing, sizes
- removing a UI element

For these, make the edit, bump `?v=`, run `node --check` on changed JS, and report. Do not restart the server unless server JS changed.

Use the browser only when a flow can actually break, or when the user asks for a test:

- sign-in and sign-up
- sending a bet to a friend
- saving, opening, or deleting parlays
- new features with clicks that change state

When the browser is needed, prefer one `Runtime.evaluate` that returns a short JSON answer over a full `browser_snapshot`. Take at most one screenshot.
